</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/4594</identifier><datestamp>2026-09-01T18:30:59Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_6</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_121</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Análise pelas resistências das enfermeiras em assumir a coordenação de enfermagem no hospital universitário: estudo  socioclínico institucional</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Ana Carolina Brito Matos</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Análise Institucional</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Prática Profissional</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Hospitais Universitários</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Educação em Enfermagem</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Enfermagem</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Dissertação Acadêmica</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Análise Institucional</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Enfermagem</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Hospital</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Introduction: In the hospital under study, there is a reluctance/resistance among nurses to assume nursing coordination roles and a limited supply of training for succession in these leadership positions, creating an organizational problem. General objective: To analyze the possible reluctance/resistance of nurses to assume the position of nursing coordinator in the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit (PICU) at a University Hospital in Minas Gerais. Methodology: This is an intervention research study conducted with 17 nurses from the PICU, using the theoretical-methodological framework of Institutional Analysis, specifically the Institutional Socioclinical approach. Data were collected using the devices “Addressed Letter”, Socioclinical Encounters, and Researcher's Diary, organized and analyzed according to the eight characteristics of Institutional Socioclinical Analysis. Results and Discussion: The analyzers “Image Clothesline”, organizational chart, time, money, and resistance revealed institutional aspects and the dynamics of the work process, as well as the institutions that influence the professional practice of nursing coordination. This analysis also identified the main reasons for resistance/refusal to assume this position, such as: lack of recognition of the nursing coordinator's role; conflict of functions with the unit's head; excessively bureaucratic processes; overload, suffering, and illness at work; lack of professional profile and specific training for this position; difficulty in executing plans; lack of financial incentives and benefits for the position; interference from the medical institution in nursing work; depletion of the work schedule; lack of support from the Nursing Division; little autonomy and governance of the coordinator; invasion of their private time; and failure in communication between sectors. Facilitating factors included team unity and engagement, as well as the nursing coordinator's proximity to the care team, while hindering factors included the hospital's vertical management structure, the biomedical model, and the managerial model adopted by the Brazilian Hospital Services Company (EBSERH). Final considerations: By creating a space for analysis and reflection on the professional practice of the nursing coordinator, the participants were able to uncover the reasons and forms of defensive, offensive, and integrative resistance to institutional factors involving the biomedical model and the vertical management model of EBSERH and the hospital itself. Thus, the technical product of this work was the intervention research itself, in addition to a complementary proposal to adapt the professional practice analysis tool called Groupe Entraînement de Analyse de Situations Éducatives (GEASE), as a form of continuing education, in order to mobilize nurses to achieve their rights and assume management positions in the hospital under study.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-09-01T18:30:59Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2026-02-23</dc:date>
   <dc:type>Dissertação de mestrado</dc:type>
   <dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/1843/4594</dc:identifier>
