</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/5777</identifier><datestamp>2026-10-16T13:24:50Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_270</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Plano de curso: incentivo à leitura de alunos do 6º ano do ensino fundamental</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Ana Kelly Barbosa Cândido</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Atividades de incentivo à leitura; plano de curso; ensino fundamental.</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>This work was carried out from a bibliographic review for the foundation of proposals about reading incentive activities to be developed in 6th grade elementary classrooms (FREIRE, 1989; GOULEMOT, 1996; KOCH and ELIAS, 2007). In this work, it is considered that reading learning should extrapolate actions that only link it to processes of acquisition of a technique: it is, above all, an activity of approximation and appropriation, in which uses, situations and social interactions build meanings in various forms of expression of human language. Finally, it is concluded that by highlighting the uses of skills that involve reading activity, the proposals worked here may stimulate interest in reading and contribute to their learning in an orderly and grounded way.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-10-16T13:24:50Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2020-01-28</dc:date>
