</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/4535</identifier><datestamp>2026-08-31T14:30:21Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_276</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Projeto de Intervenção para minimizar e monitorar a ocorrência de parasitoses intestinais em Crianças da UBS São Gregório</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Joelson Fernando Atanazo Brasileiro Mendonça</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Atenção Primária à Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Saúde Pública</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Saúde da Criança</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Saúde da Família</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Determinantes Sociais da Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Política de Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Saneamento</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Monitoramento Epidemiológico</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Equipe de Assistência ao Paciente</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Atenção à Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Promoção da Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Planos e Programas de Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Estratégias de Saúde Nacionais</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Programas de Rastreamento</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>doenças parasitárias</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>atenção primária à saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>educação em saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Intestinal parasites are an important public health problem in Brazil, with a high prevalence in the child population, especially in territories marked by socio-environmental vulnerabilities. Its persistence is associated with structural determinants, such as poor sanitation, low education and limitations in health literacy, which requires integrated approaches that go beyond isolated clinical treatment. This work aims to analyze and support an action plan for the prevention, control and care of intestinal parasites in children enrolled at the São Gregório Family Health Unit, in light of the principles of Primary Health Care and the Family Health Strategy. This is a descriptive and interventional study, based on a review of scientific literature and normative documents of the Unified Health System, focusing on educational actions in health, clinical-laboratory tracking, epidemiological surveillance, systematic case recording and intersectoral coordination. It is expected that the implementation of the proposed actions will contribute to increasing the knowledge of children and families about preventive measures, qualifying longitudinal monitoring, strengthening local surveillance and greater integration between health, education and municipal management. It is concluded that the sustainable fight against intestinal parasites in the child population depends on the articulated work of the PHC multidisciplinary team, the active adherence of the clientele and intersectoral action on the social determinants of health, reaffirming the strategic role of Primary Care in comprehensive care for children’s health.</dc:description>
