</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/62196</identifier><datestamp>2026-08-12T03:00:14Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_200</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Design de sistema de gestão processual na 18ª vara cível de Belo Horizonte: estreita relação entre teoria e prática</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Marco Antônio de Melo</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Minas Gerais - Tribunal de Justiça</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Processo civil - Brasil</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Poder judiciário - Brasil</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Organização judiciária</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Gestão processual</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Prática</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Vara cível</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Movimentação de processos</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Inovações</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>The theme of the research developed here, intends to present the procedural management model applied in the 18th Civil Court of Belo Horizonte/MG, from 2013 to 2022. Its primary objective, however, is to reveal the close relationship between the theory, taught in course in Systems Design Applied to Conflict Resolution and Process Management, offered by the Faculty of Law of the Federal University of Minas Gerais in partnership with the Escola Judicial Des. Edésio Fernandes from TJMG and the practice, experienced on a daily basis in a jurisdictional unit in the capital of Minas Gerais. This research thus emphatically addresses the panorama found in the judicial unit, because it was in this court that the researcher was a judge for approximately 10 years and where he experienced the most challenging situations of his career. magistrate. And it is in this context that a true justification for the present work can be found, namely, in the need to demonstrate that the knowledge absorbed in the aforementioned course can prove, in practice, to be a true tool to face the distressing challenge excessive litigation, a phenomenon that seriously concerns the Brazilian judiciary. The proposed investigation will be conducted mainly through comparative analysis of procedural movements and graphs made available by the SIJUD system of the Court of Justice of Minas Gerais. This research, finally, also has, even if modestly, the ambitious expectation that its findings may help other magistrates in the management of their jurisdictional units, since the number of cases continues to present high rates on scales never before reached. previously imagined and the situations portrayed here are frequent.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2023-12-28T11:34:19Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2025-09-08T23:01:00Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2023-12-28T11:34:19Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2023-10-30</dc:date>
