   <dc:title>Avanços e transformações no sistema de inovação de Minas Gerais</dc:title>
   <dc:title>Advances and transformations in the innovation system of Minas Gerais</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Márcia Siqueira Rapini</dc:creator>
   <dc:creator>João Francisco Sarno Carvalho</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Economia</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Inovação</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Minas Gerais</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>sistema de inovação</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>sistema regional de inovação</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Minas Gerais</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Over the last twenty years, several public and private initiatives have sought to support technological innovation in Brazil, with particular emphasis on the Technological Innovation Law, which completed two decades in 2024. This study asks: what institutional and organizational changes have occurred in the Minas Gerais Innovation System over the last twenty years? To answer this question, a qualitative and descriptive study was conducted using primary and secondary data from official federal, state, and municipal databases, as well as from public and private institutions. Data analysis, carried out using Microsoft Excel and Philcarto, revealed the creation of new educational institutions, the enactment of innovative laws, and the formation of public–private partnerships to foster startups. However, the Minas Gerais innovation system still faces challenges, such as regional inequalities and structural immaturity. In this sense, the results of this study may contribute to the improvement of public policies and institutional strategies aimed at strengthening the innovation ecosystem and reducing regional inequalities in the state of Minas Gerais.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-10-16T00:34:16Z</dc:date>
