</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/5486</identifier><datestamp>2026-10-06T14:49:36Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_180</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>O novo paradigma das nulidades em contratos públicos: da rigidez formal à visão consequencialista</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Hamilton Roque Miranda Pires</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Direito administrativo - Brasil</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Nulidade</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Contrato público - Legislação - Brasil</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Garantia (Direito)</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Licitação pública</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Nulidades administrativas</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Consequencialismo</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>LINDB</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Lei nº 14.133/2021</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Contratações públicas</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Segurança jurídica</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>This study examines the evolution of the legal agenda governing nullities in Brazilian public procurement and administrative contracts, analyzing the transition from the traditional model - characterized by formalism and the automatic invalidation of administrative acts and contracts - to the consequentialist paradigm consolidated by Law No. 13.655/2018 and materialized in the Law No. 14.133/2021. The research is guided by the following problem: to what extent has the new Public Procurement and Administrative Contracts Law transformed the classical nullity regime by replacing the logic of automatic invalidation with an approach focused on the practical consequences of administrative decisions? To address this question, a legal-dogmatic methodology was adopted, based on bibliographical, legislative, and documentary research, encompassing the analysis of specialized legal scholarship, relevant legislation, and jurisprudential developments related to the subject. The study begins with a historical reconstruction of the traditional nullity regime and its main challenges, examining the influence of administrative formalism and the consolidation of the ex tunc approach under Law No. 8.666/1993. It then explores the gradual flexibilization of this model, highlighting the contributions of Law No. 9.784/1999 and the evolution of judicial and administrative case law. Subsequently, the research analyzes the incorporation of consequentialism into Brazilian Public Law through Law No. 13.655/2018, particularly articles 20 and 21 of the Brazilian Law of Introduction to the Norms of Brazilian Law (LINDB), demonstrating its effects on the theory of administrative nullities. Finally, the study investigates how these principles were incorporated into Law No. 14.133/2021, with emphasis on corrective measures, the multi-factor analysis of public interest, contractual continuity, compensation for losses and damages, and the temporal modulation of the effects of nullity. The study concludes that Law No. 14.133/2021 has significantly transformed the legal regime of nullities in public procurement, replacing the primacy of formalism with the concept of functional legality, which requires decision-makers to assess the concrete impacts of invalidating administrative acts and contracts. The new framework seeks to reconcile legality, legal certainty, administrative efficiency, and the protection of legitimate expectations, thereby fostering more rational administrative decisions and strengthening the continuity of public policies and contracts serving the collective interest.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-10-06T14:49:36Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2026-06-03</dc:date>
   <dc:type>Monografia de especialização</dc:type>
