</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/4915</identifier><datestamp>2026-09-16T12:27:45Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_6</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_246</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>A concordância verbal e nominal no Ensino Médio: entre a norma padrão e a variedade linguística dos estudantes</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Amanda Cristina Da Silva</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Língua portuguesa Estudo e ensino</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Língua portuguesa Gramática</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Ensino de língua portuguesa; Gramática; Concordância verbal e nominal; Ensino Médio</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Grammar is highly valued in various contexts and has long been used as an instrument of power. That said, discussions about linguistic variety are essential; because language is not immutable, as it can be altered according to social, regional, historical factors, level of education, among others. Thus, we cannot invalidate these particularities of language, specifically the Portuguese language spoken in Brazil, given that this is a large and culturally rich country. All existing varieties, in addition to the standard language, can be studied in grammar teaching in schools. This research is a descriptive study that aims to elaborate and develop a grammar teaching proposal that enables high school students to value the grammar of use in their interactions, understand the reasons for varieties, and know the grammar necessary for using the language in formal and informal situations. Descriptive research observes and evaluates the behaviors of a group of individuals without influencing them; therefore, the students were the agents and scientists of this research. Thus, this proposal was applied to class 3001, in the 3rd year of high school at the Juscelino Kubitschek State School, in the Durval de Barros neighborhood - Ibirité. Therefore, it is important for students to understand that their way of speaking has value, but that society demands the use of formal language. Without it, this individual will hardly
change their social, economic, and professional situation. The objective was to make them understand the need to master more than one variety: the one they speak in their social context, the one spoken in scientific, academic, and formal settings, and even the one that only individuals belonging to a specific group understand. The classes contributed to the students' learning, as they better understood the function of words within the phrase and how to use verbal and nominal agreement in situations that require the more formal use of language. Furthermore, the students understood that even in the most informal sentences there are rules, and they know how to use them. However, the research presented some challenges, as the students' first instinct was to correct any incorrect sentence that appeared. The methodology employed was developed from a qualitative and interventional perspective, aiming to map expressions present in oral texts constructed by the students themselves, with the objective of creating a list of rules for their variety. The theoretical foundation is based on the studies of Costa Val (2002), Irandé Antunes (2014), Geraldi (2005), Duarte (2015), and Vieira (2018). The goal was for students to become familiar with existing varieties and be able to navigate different social contexts, should they wish to do so.</dc:description>
   <dc:description>CAPES - Coordenação de Aperfeiçoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-09-16T12:27:45Z</dc:date>
