</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/5167</identifier><datestamp>2026-09-25T17:50:31Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_6</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_381</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Desempenho cognitivo (MoCA) em mulheres na pós-menopausa cirúrgica e espontânea com ou sem thm: estudo de corte transversal</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Simone Floresta Leal</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Disfunção Cognitiva</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Terapia de Reposição de Estrogênios</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Ovariectomia</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Cognição</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Dissertação Acadêmica</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Declínio cognitivo leve</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Terapia hormonal da menopausa</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Ooforectomia</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Função cognitiva</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>MoCA</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>Mild cognitive impairment (MCI) is a condition that can precede dementia and significantly impact quality of life. Factors such as age, educational level, and hormonal changes play a crucial role in its development. Among women, oophorectomy, whether spontaneous or surgical, and the consequent reduction in hormone levels may be associated with an increased risk of cognitive impairment.
This study aimed to investigate the relationship between hormone replacement therapy (HRT) and cognitive performance in women who underwent oophorectomy. Women with and without HRT were assessed using the Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA) test, considering specific cognitive domains. Additionally, predictive and protective factors for MCI within this group were analyzed.
The results suggest that hormone therapy may play a protective role in cognitive function, especially in the early years after menopause or oophorectomy. Furthermore, educational level proved to be a relevant factor in preserving cognitive functions. These findings highlight the importance of individualized follow-up for women undergoing oophorectomy, considering both the impact of hormone therapy and other cognitive and clinical factors.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-09-25T17:50:31Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2026-01-28</dc:date>
   <dc:type>Dissertação de mestrado</dc:type>
   <dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/1843/5167</dc:identifier>
