</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/3601</identifier><datestamp>2026-07-22T13:30:54Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_397</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Encontros e desencontros de uma professora-artista</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Ana Carolina de Sena Sant'Ana</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Arte - Estudo e ensino</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Arte e educação</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Ensino de arte</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Identidade docente</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Prática artística</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Arte-educação</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>The final project aims to analyze the relationship between being a teacher and being an artist, investigating how teaching practices in Art intersect with artistic processes within the school environment. This research arises from questions about the multiple roles played by an Art teacher and the challenges this position poses to exploring artistic expression—both that of the students and of the teacher herself. The central question of this study is: “What does it mean to be an artist?” Although this question may not have a definitive answer, it opens space for reflections on Art education and the artist's identity within the school context. The theoretical framework is based on three main references: Rick Rubin, who emphasizes artistic sensitivity; Viviane Diehl, who proposes a hybrid figure between educator and artist; and Kamila Debortoli, who discusses pedagogical relationships and the notion of talent. A parallel is also drawn between these authors and the artist Thais Antonoff, a contemporary art educator and creator of the @infanciacomarte page, who reflects on the challenges and enchantments of being a “prof-artist.” Thus, this work seeks to understand how an artist can be a teacher and how a teacher can be an artist without compromising their essence and creativity, considering the demands of the school routine. Moreover, it highlights the difficulties encountered in teaching practice and reinforces the importance of moments of creative idleness and imagination in Art education.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-07-22T13:30:54Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2025-08-05</dc:date>
   <dc:type>Monografia de especialização</dc:type>
