</metadata></record><record><header><identifier>oai:repositorio.ufmg.br:1843/4528</identifier><datestamp>2026-08-31T12:39:42Z</datestamp><setSpec>com_1843_5</setSpec><setSpec>com_1843_2</setSpec><setSpec>col_1843_276</setSpec></header><metadata><oai_dc:dc xmlns:oai_dc="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:doc="http://www.lyncode.com/xoai" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc/ http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/oai_dc.xsd">
   <dc:title>Letramento em saúde na Atenção Primária à Saúde: um Projeto de Intervenção para qualificação da comunicação e do cuidado</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Ana Gabrielle Rodrigues de Souza Rocha</dc:creator>
   <dc:subject>Atenção Primária à Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Literacia para a Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Autocuidado</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Nível de Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Equipe de Assistência ao Paciente</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Educação em Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Autoimagem</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Comunicação</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Educação Continuada</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Conhecimentos, Atitudes e Prática em Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Compreensão</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Pessoal de Saúde</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Estratégias de Saúde Nacionais</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Cooperação e Adesão ao Tratamento</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Escolaridade</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Health education</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Shared decision making</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Therapeutic adherence</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>A low educational level is an important social determinant of health and has a direct influence on health literacy, self-perception of the health-disease process and adherence to therapies proposed in Primary Health Care (PHC). In the territory covered by the Raimunda Maria da Conceição Family Health Strategy, it is observed that limitations related to the educational level of the adult and elderly population negatively impact the understanding of health guidelines, favoring the overuse of services and low therapeutic adherence. This work aims to analyze the influence of health literacy on the care offered in PHC and implement an Intervention Project aimed at qualifying communication between health professionals and users. The methodology consists of a review of scientific literature, ongoing education of the multidisciplinary team, development and application of educational health tools with accessible language, in addition to evaluating their applicability in the territory. It is expected that the intervention will contribute to improving users’ understanding of their health conditions, strengthening autonomy in self-care, qualifying the team’s work process and greater resolution of care in Primary Health Care.</dc:description>
   <dc:date>2026-08-31T12:39:42Z</dc:date>
   <dc:date>2026-02-23</dc:date>
   <dc:type>Monografia de especialização</dc:type>
   <dc:identifier>https://hdl.handle.net/1843/4528</dc:identifier>
   <dc:language>por</dc:language>
   <dc:rights>Acesso aberto</dc:rights>
